Now I have a complete understanding of the file. Let me design the full implementation plan.

---

## Implementation Plan: Boldteq Docs Dashboard Redesign

### 1. Overall Architecture

The file is 1207 lines with a single export `BoldteqSaasFlowSetup` and 18 helper components. The redesign keeps the single-file approach but restructures the main component into a documentation dashboard with fixed topbar, fixed sidebar, and a scrollable content area that shows one section at a time (page-based navigation instead of scroll-based).

---

### 2. New Import Requirements

Add to existing Lucide imports:
- `Search` (for search bar icon)
- `ChevronDown` / `ChevronRight` (for collapsible sidebar groups)
- `X` (for closing search modal)
- `Command` (for Cmd+K hint badge)
- `BookOpen` (for breadcrumb/logo area)
- `Menu` (optional, for mobile toggle)

The existing imports (`useState`) need `useEffect`, `useRef`, `useMemo`, and `useCallback` added from React.

---

### 3. State Management - Exact Shape

Replace the current two-state setup with:

```js
const [activePage, setActivePage] = useState("overview");
const [searchOpen, setSearchOpen] = useState(false);
const [searchQuery, setSearchQuery] = useState("");
const [collapsedGroups, setCollapsedGroups] = useState({});
const [checkedItems, setCheckedItems] = useState({});
```

`activePage` replaces `activeSection`. The scroll-to-element behavior on sidebar click is removed entirely; instead, clicking a sidebar item sets `activePage` and the content area renders only that section.

---

### 4. Sidebar Group Structure - Exact Data

Define this constant outside the component (or inside with `useMemo`):

```js
const SIDEBAR_GROUPS = [
  {
    name: "Getting Started",
    icon: BookOpen,    // or Layers
    sections: [
      { id: "overview", label: "Overview", icon: Layers },
      { id: "stack", label: "Stack A", icon: Terminal },
    ],
  },
  {
    name: "Infrastructure",
    icon: Server,
    sections: [
      { id: "mapping", label: "Env Mapping", icon: GitBranch },
      { id: "flow", label: "Deploy Flow", icon: ArrowRight },
      { id: "github", label: "GitHub", icon: GitPullRequest },
      { id: "railway", label: "Railway", icon: Train },
      { id: "supabase", label: "Supabase", icon: Database },
    ],
  },
  {
    name: "Security & Payments",
    icon: Shield,
    sections: [
      { id: "auth", label: "Auth & Security", icon: ShieldCheck },
      { id: "billing", label: "Billing", icon: CreditCard },
    ],
  },
  {
    name: "Operations",
    icon: Activity,
    sections: [
      { id: "monitoring", label: "Monitoring", icon: Activity },
      { id: "gates", label: "Quality Gates", icon: CheckCircle },
      { id: "rules", label: "Non-Negotiables", icon: Lock },
    ],
  },
  {
    name: "Setup",
    icon: ClipboardCheck,
    sections: [
      { id: "checklist", label: "Setup Checklist", icon: ClipboardCheck },
      { id: "changelog", label: "Changelog", icon: FileText },
    ],
  },
];
```

The `collapsedGroups` state uses group name as key. Default: all groups expanded (empty object or all `false`). Toggle function:

```js
const toggleGroup = (groupName) => {
  setCollapsedGroups(prev => ({ ...prev, [groupName]: !prev[groupName] }));
};
```

---

### 5. Search Index - Structure and Building

Build a flat searchable array using `useMemo`. Each entry has the shape:

```js
{ text: string, section: string, sectionId: string, type: string }
```

Where `type` is one of: `"title"`, `"rule"`, `"checklist"`, `"tech"`, `"forbidden"`, `"security"`, `"gate"`.

The index must be built from the same data arrays currently inlined in the JSX. The key refactoring step: **extract all data arrays into named constants at the top of the file**, outside the component. This serves both the search index and the render. Specifically extract:

- `TECH_STACK` - the 12-item array at line 187-199
- `HARD_RULES` - the 15 rules at line 254-269
- `FORBIDDEN_ITEMS` - the 12 items at line 281-292
- `SECURITY_CHECKLIST` - the 10 items at line 557-573
- `NON_NEGOTIABLES` - the 14 rules at line 718-741
- `QUALITY_GATES` - the 4 gate objects with their checks at line 664-710
- `DEPLOY_STEPS` - the 7 steps at line 336-348
- `MONITORING_TOOLS` - the 4 tools at line 616-627
- `CHECKLIST_GROUPS_DATA` - all 6 checklist groups with their items (lines 749-836)

Then the search index:

```js
const searchIndex = useMemo(() => {
  const items = [];

  // Section titles
  SIDEBAR_GROUPS.forEach(group => {
    group.sections.forEach(s => {
      items.push({ text: s.label, section: s.label, sectionId: s.id, type: "title" });
    });
  });

  // Tech stack
  TECH_STACK.forEach(t => {
    items.push({ text: `${t.name} ${t.version} - ${t.role}`, section: "Stack A", sectionId: "stack", type: "tech" });
  });

  // Hard rules
  HARD_RULES.forEach(r => {
    items.push({ text: r, section: "Stack A", sectionId: "stack", type: "rule" });
  });

  // Forbidden items
  FORBIDDEN_ITEMS.forEach(f => {
    items.push({ text: f, section: "Stack A", sectionId: "stack", type: "forbidden" });
  });

  // Security checklist
  SECURITY_CHECKLIST.forEach(s => {
    items.push({ text: s, section: "Auth & Security", sectionId: "auth", type: "security" });
  });

  // Non-negotiables
  NON_NEGOTIABLES.forEach(r => {
    items.push({ text: r, section: "Non-Negotiables", sectionId: "rules", type: "rule" });
  });

  // Quality gate checks
  QUALITY_GATES.forEach(g => {
    g.checks.forEach(c => {
      items.push({ text: c, section: "Quality Gates", sectionId: "gates", type: "gate" });
    });
  });

  // Checklist items
  CHECKLIST_GROUPS_DATA.forEach(g => {
    g.items.forEach(item => {
      items.push({ text: item, section: "Setup Checklist", sectionId: "checklist", type: "checklist" });
    });
  });

  return items;
}, []);
```

Filtering logic:

```js
const searchResults = useMemo(() => {
  if (!searchQuery.trim()) return [];
  const q = searchQuery.toLowerCase();
  const matches = searchIndex.filter(item => item.text.toLowerCase().includes(q));

  // Group by section
  const grouped = {};
  matches.forEach(m => {
    if (!grouped[m.section]) grouped[m.section] = [];
    grouped[m.section].push(m);
  });
  return grouped;
}, [searchQuery, searchIndex]);
```

---

### 6. Keyboard Shortcut Implementation

Use `useEffect` with a global keydown listener:

```js
useEffect(() => {
  const handler = (e) => {
    if ((e.metaKey || e.ctrlKey) && e.key === "k") {
      e.preventDefault();
      setSearchOpen(prev => !prev);
      setSearchQuery("");
    }
    if (e.key === "Escape") {
      setSearchOpen(false);
      setSearchQuery("");
    }
  };
  document.addEventListener("keydown", handler);
  return () => document.removeEventListener("keydown", handler);
}, []);
```

Also auto-focus the search input when the modal opens, using a ref:

```js
const searchInputRef = useRef(null);
useEffect(() => {
  if (searchOpen && searchInputRef.current) {
    searchInputRef.current.focus();
  }
}, [searchOpen]);
```

---

### 7. Layout CSS - Fixed Sidebar + Topbar, Scrollable Content

The current layout uses `max-w-7xl mx-auto grid grid-cols-12`. Replace with a full-viewport fixed layout:

```
+-----------------------------------------------+
| TOPBAR (fixed top, full width, h-14, z-30)    |
+----------+------------------------------------+
| SIDEBAR  | CONTENT AREA                       |
| (fixed   | (scrollable, margin-left: 260px,   |
|  left,   |  margin-top: 56px)                 |
|  w-[260] |  max-w-4xl centered in remaining   |
|  top-14, |  space)                             |
|  h-full, |                                     |
|  z-20)   |                                     |
+----------+------------------------------------+
```

Main wrapper structure:

```jsx
<div className="min-h-screen bg-slate-50">
  <Topbar onSearchOpen={() => setSearchOpen(true)} />
  <Sidebar 
    groups={SIDEBAR_GROUPS} 
    activePage={activePage} 
    onNavigate={setActivePage}
    collapsedGroups={collapsedGroups}
    onToggleGroup={toggleGroup}
  />
  <main className="ml-[260px] mt-14 min-h-[calc(100vh-56px)]">
    <div className="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-8 py-8">
      <Breadcrumb activePage={activePage} groups={SIDEBAR_GROUPS} />
      {/* Conditional section rendering */}
      {activePage === "overview" && <OverviewContent />}
      {activePage === "stack" && <StackContent />}
      {/* ... etc for all 14 sections */}
    </div>
  </main>
  {searchOpen && <SearchModal ... />}
</div>
```

---

### 8. Component Breakdown - New Components

**Topbar** (~30 lines):
- Fixed `top-0 left-0 right-0 h-14 bg-white border-b border-slate-200 z-30`
- Left: Logo text "Boldteq Docs" in serif font with indigo dot
- Center: Search trigger button styled as a fake input (`bg-slate-100 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 w-80`) showing "Search documentation..." with a `Cmd+K` badge on the right. Clicking opens modal.
- Right: Version badge `v2.0.0` in a pill, and status indicator

**Sidebar** (~60 lines):
- Fixed `top-14 left-0 bottom-0 w-[260px] bg-white border-r border-slate-200 z-20 overflow-y-auto`
- Padding: `py-4 px-3`
- Each group renders: a clickable header row with `ChevronDown`/`ChevronRight` icon, group name in `text-xs tracking-widest text-slate-400 font-medium uppercase`
- When expanded, show section links below with left padding. Each link: `flex items-center gap-2 text-sm py-2 px-3 rounded-lg`. Active state: `bg-indigo-50 text-indigo-700 font-medium`. Inactive: `text-slate-600 hover:bg-slate-100`
- Keep the "PRINCIPLE" quote box at the bottom of the sidebar

**SearchModal** (~60 lines):
- Fixed overlay: `fixed inset-0 z-50 flex items-start justify-center pt-[15vh]`
- Backdrop: `fixed inset-0 bg-black/20 backdrop-blur-sm` with onClick to close
- Modal: `bg-white rounded-xl shadow-2xl w-full max-w-lg border border-slate-200 overflow-hidden`
- Input at top: full-width, `text-lg p-4 border-b`, with Search icon left and Escape hint right
- Results area below: max-height `max-h-[60vh] overflow-y-auto`
- Results grouped by section name as headers (`text-xs text-slate-400 tracking-widest uppercase px-4 pt-3`)
- Each result item: clickable row (`px-4 py-2.5 hover:bg-indigo-50 cursor-pointer`), showing item text truncated, with a small type badge. Clicking sets `activePage` to the result's `sectionId` and closes the modal.
- Empty state: "No results found" centered text
- Initial state (no query): show section titles as quick-nav options

**Breadcrumb** (~15 lines):
- Find which group the `activePage` belongs to
- Render: `Group Name / Section Name` in small text with `/` separator
- Style: `text-xs text-slate-400 mb-6 flex items-center gap-2`
- Group name is clickable (navigates to first section in group)

---

### 9. Page-Based Content Rendering

Remove the `<main className="space-y-20">` that renders all sections. Instead, conditionally render only the active section. The simplest pattern:

```jsx
const renderContent = () => {
  switch (activePage) {
    case "overview": return <OverviewSection />;
    case "stack": return <StackSection />;
    // ... all 14 cases
    default: return <OverviewSection />;
  }
};
```

Each section's JSX stays exactly as-is (lines 141-870), just wrapped in a function component or extracted into the switch. The `<section id="...">` wrapper and `scroll-mt-8` class are no longer needed since there is no scrolling to anchors.

The `scrollIntoView` call in the current sidebar click handler (line 115) is removed entirely.

---

### 10. Data Extraction - What Moves Where

Move these inline arrays to constants defined above the component (approximately lines 26-45 area, before the component function):

| Constant Name | Current Location (line) | Used In Section |
|---|---|---|
| `TECH_STACK` | 187-199 | stack |
| `RAILWAY_SERVICES` | 212-217 | stack |
| `SUPABASE_BACKEND` | 232-237 | stack |
| `HARD_RULES` | 254-269 | stack |
| `FORBIDDEN_ITEMS` | 281-292 | stack |
| `DEPLOY_STEPS` | 336-348 | flow |
| `SECURITY_CHECKLIST` | 557-573 | auth |
| `MONITORING_TOOLS` | 616-627 | monitoring |
| `PERF_TARGETS` | 644-649 | monitoring |
| `NON_NEGOTIABLES` | 718-741 | rules |
| `QUALITY_GATES` | 664-710 (structured) | gates |
| `SETUP_CHECKLISTS` | 749-836 (6 groups) | checklist |
| `CHANGELOG_ENTRIES` | 844-868 | changelog |

This is the most labor-intensive part of the refactor but critical for making content searchable.

---

### 11. Scroll Reset on Page Change

When `activePage` changes, scroll the content area to top:

```js
useEffect(() => {
  const content = document.getElementById("content-area");
  if (content) content.scrollTop = 0;
}, [activePage]);
```

Or, if the `<main>` uses the window scroll, simply `window.scrollTo(0, 0)`.

---

### 12. Implementation Sequence (Step by Step)

**Step 1 - Extract data constants** (~20 min)
Move all inline data arrays to named constants above the component. Verify rendering is unchanged.

**Step 2 - Add new state variables** (~5 min)
Add `searchOpen`, `searchQuery`, `collapsedGroups` to state. Rename `activeSection` to `activePage`.

**Step 3 - Build the layout shell** (~15 min)
Replace the current `header` + `grid` layout with the fixed topbar + fixed sidebar + scrollable main structure. At this point, content temporarily breaks.

**Step 4 - Implement Topbar component** (~10 min)
Extract the logo, search trigger, and version info into a `Topbar` component.

**Step 5 - Implement Sidebar component** (~15 min)
Build the collapsible group sidebar using `SIDEBAR_GROUPS`. Wire up `activePage` navigation and `collapsedGroups` toggle.

**Step 6 - Implement page-based rendering** (~10 min)
Replace the single `<main>` that renders all sections with the conditional switch/map. Each section renders only when it is the active page.

**Step 7 - Implement Breadcrumb** (~5 min)
Simple component that looks up the active page in `SIDEBAR_GROUPS` and renders `Group > Section`.

**Step 8 - Build search index** (~10 min)
Create the `useMemo` search index from all extracted data constants.

**Step 9 - Implement SearchModal** (~20 min)
Build the overlay modal with input, grouped results, navigation on click, and escape-to-close.

**Step 10 - Implement Cmd+K shortcut** (~5 min)
Add the `useEffect` keydown listener.

